anubis source for Keel Linux
============================

Branches
--------

debian/sid   the Debian Go team's work-in-progress packaging, as on salsa
             (go-team/packages/anubis, ITP #1102132), unchanged
upstream     upstream imports; its history includes upstream's git history
keel/trixie  this package, built for the Keel repository

The layout is DEP-14's, with the tags upstream/<version> and
keel/<debian-version>. `gbp buildpackage` builds both orig tarballs from
the upstream/<version> tag (there is no pristine-tar branch: the npm
component is assembled, not released), and `dpkg-buildpackage -b` from a
clone of keel/trixie works too, since the upstream branch carries
everything the build reads.

Upstream tarball and the npm component
--------------------------------------

The main tarball is upstream's anubis-src-vendor-VERSION.tar.gz from the
GitHub release, which already contains vendor/ (go mod vendor), signed
with the key in debian/upstream/signing-key.asc:

  gpgv --keyring debian/upstream/signing-key.asc \
      anubis-src-vendor-VERSION.tar.gz.asc anubis-src-vendor-VERSION.tar.gz

The npm component (npm/, the "npm" component of gbp.conf) holds the
runtime JavaScript dependencies that esbuild bundles into the challenge
pages; nothing from npm/ is installed as is. They are the closure of
"preact" and "@aws-crypto/sha256-js" in package-lock.json:

  preact, @aws-crypto/sha256-js, @aws-crypto/util, @aws-sdk/types,
  @smithy/is-array-buffer, @smithy/types, @smithy/util-buffer-from,
  @smithy/util-utf8, tslib

To refresh it for a new upstream version, download each "resolved" URL of
package-lock.json, check it against its "integrity" (sha512, base64), and
unpack each tarball's package/ directory into npm/<name>. The development
dependencies (esbuild, postcss, cssnano, playwright, ...) are not needed:
esbuild comes from Debian and the CSS is bundled with esbuild.

Generated files
---------------

The build regenerates the templ and stringer output with the vendored
tools (go generate) and builds all JavaScript and CSS from source. The
precompressed .gz, .zst and .br copies that web/build.sh writes are
embedded but never served (anubis compresses on the fly).

Towards Debian
--------------

Debian's Go team packages each module separately instead of vendoring;
see debian/TODO.Debian for what remains before this can converge with
the ITP.
